WEBVTT

00:05.255 --> 00:11.261
‪RAMUNE

00:23.606 --> 00:24.816
- Shige.
- Yeah?

00:24.899 --> 00:25.942
- Please try this.
- Okay.

00:27.736 --> 00:29.404
Is this kinpira?

00:29.946 --> 00:30.989
Yes.

00:34.617 --> 00:36.536
Yeah, I think it's good.

00:36.619 --> 00:38.079
Thank you.

00:40.999 --> 00:44.753
You've stopped… making Korean appetizers.

00:45.336 --> 00:46.171
Huh?

00:47.130 --> 00:49.466
Our customers loved them.
They were really good.

00:50.717 --> 00:51.593
Sorry…

00:56.556 --> 00:58.808
- Can I get a refill on my shochu?
- Yes.

00:58.892 --> 00:59.768
A shochu refill.

00:59.851 --> 01:00.769
Okay.

01:05.940 --> 01:06.983
Welcome.

01:07.942 --> 01:09.444
Good to see you!

01:18.495 --> 01:19.496
Welcome.

01:20.080 --> 01:21.498
Hello.

01:21.581 --> 01:23.083
I brought the files
that I was talking about.

01:24.375 --> 01:26.711
- I'll get a drink and wait for you.
- Okay.

01:52.445 --> 01:54.197
SCORCHED RICE FLAVOR

02:03.998 --> 02:05.667
It's not working at all…

02:21.516 --> 02:23.226
Did you eat?

02:28.857 --> 02:31.192
You don't have to come here every day.

02:33.153 --> 02:36.823
I have tomorrow off,
so I can hang out with you all night.

02:44.164 --> 02:44.998
Let's go.

04:02.450 --> 04:03.493
Here.

04:04.661 --> 04:05.703
Thanks.

04:13.670 --> 04:16.172
That's right, you can't do spicy, huh?

04:16.839 --> 04:17.757
It's too spicy.

04:31.813 --> 04:33.731
Jun-ho, your eyes are half closed.

04:37.902 --> 04:39.112
We should head home soon.

04:45.451 --> 04:47.245
What's wrong?

04:48.705 --> 04:50.248
I'm sorry.

04:50.832 --> 04:52.542
Can I borrow you for a bit longer?

04:54.544 --> 04:56.629
I just had so much fun today.

05:02.427 --> 05:04.053
When I'm alone,

05:04.137 --> 05:06.973
I can't stop thinking about Taiga.

05:12.895 --> 05:15.148
Just one more drink. Please?

05:15.231 --> 05:16.065
It's on me.

05:16.691 --> 05:17.817
Okay? Just one more.

05:18.568 --> 05:19.610
- Shall we?
- Let's go!

05:25.325 --> 05:29.162
The sports magazine Clayton
is holding an anniversary party.

05:29.245 --> 05:30.079
CLAYTON'S ANNIVERSARY PARTY

05:30.163 --> 05:34.709
The editor-in-chief of this magazine was
at the reception you did the other day.

05:34.792 --> 05:35.626
I see.

05:35.710 --> 05:40.214
The soup that you served…

05:40.298 --> 05:41.632
um…

05:41.716 --> 05:42.592
Dak gomtang?

05:42.675 --> 05:45.303
That's the one!
He really liked your dak gomtang.

05:45.887 --> 05:48.181
He wants you to serve that
at this party too.

05:48.890 --> 05:49.932
What do you think?

05:53.728 --> 05:55.605
Is there a problem?

05:56.355 --> 05:58.274
No, it's fine.

05:58.357 --> 05:59.817
I'd love to do this.

05:59.901 --> 06:01.277
I'm glad.

06:01.360 --> 06:04.947
- I'll ask Shige too. And I'll read this.
- Okay.

06:07.075 --> 06:09.827
I almost forgot.
Did you get notified about the reunion?

06:10.912 --> 06:11.746
Yeah…

06:14.123 --> 06:15.958
You won't be coming again this year?

06:18.544 --> 06:19.754
Yeah…

06:48.616 --> 06:49.742
Are you serious…

07:05.299 --> 07:06.259
I can't anymore…

07:06.342 --> 07:07.510
Let's break up.

07:31.075 --> 07:34.996
ITO SHINTARO:
SO ARE YOU COMING TO THE REUNION?

07:39.125 --> 07:41.043
I wanted you to look at me

07:41.127 --> 07:45.798
I wanted you to pay attention to me

07:45.882 --> 07:50.928
Will you please stay by my side?

07:51.012 --> 07:54.640
I like you

07:54.724 --> 07:57.935
She really doesn't try to hide
that she's sad about the breakup.

07:59.228 --> 08:00.730
I wish I could be that open.

08:05.151 --> 08:06.444
Hey…

08:06.527 --> 08:08.070
You're not going to ask Rin out?

08:10.656 --> 08:11.491
You like her, right?

08:13.534 --> 08:17.246
As long as Rin is happy,
that's all that matters.

08:18.039 --> 08:19.332
Really…

08:20.082 --> 08:23.002
You can't be the one to make her happy?

08:23.711 --> 08:24.795
Please…

08:25.963 --> 08:27.089
Stop!

08:37.058 --> 08:38.476
Put it on here, please.

08:38.559 --> 08:40.269
Thank you.

09:07.588 --> 09:08.673
I like you.

09:15.179 --> 09:17.640
"I like you." Or something like that?

09:25.606 --> 09:26.774
Sorry for poking fun at you.

09:33.990 --> 09:39.036
Rin only sees me as family.

09:40.538 --> 09:41.914
If I tell her how I feel,

09:42.623 --> 09:44.333
she will have no one else

09:45.835 --> 09:47.628
to rely on in Japan.

09:50.923 --> 09:52.049
Hey…

09:52.550 --> 09:55.052
Want me to take Rin home?

09:56.679 --> 09:57.555
What?

09:58.222 --> 09:59.849
She can sleep at my place.

10:04.061 --> 10:05.271
Thank you.

10:06.856 --> 10:09.400
To be honest, I didn't think

10:09.483 --> 10:13.029
I could stand to hear her say,
"Taiga" anymore.

10:16.157 --> 10:17.533
I see…

10:30.504 --> 10:32.131
Smells good…

10:42.141 --> 10:44.393
You're awake? Want to eat?

10:45.645 --> 10:46.479
Yeah.

10:47.104 --> 10:48.272
I will.

10:54.362 --> 10:55.780
It's ramyeon!

10:56.822 --> 10:58.532
Ramyeon?

10:58.616 --> 10:59.575
Like ramen?

10:59.659 --> 11:00.993
Yeah.

11:01.077 --> 11:04.413
There are a lot of words that are
similar in Japanese and Korean.

11:04.497 --> 11:06.957
Really? Like what?

11:07.041 --> 11:11.128
Family, promise, ignore, impossible, free.

11:11.879 --> 11:13.547
Wow, I understand all of them!

11:14.173 --> 11:15.424
That's funny.

11:19.762 --> 11:22.598
Taiga also learned Korean words for me…

11:25.351 --> 11:27.853
All right, all right.
Forget about that for now.

11:29.188 --> 11:31.857
The ramen is ready,
so get eggs from the fridge.

11:42.993 --> 11:44.245
But you know…

11:45.162 --> 11:47.540
I'm kind of envious

11:47.623 --> 11:52.503
of how you're so
honest with your feelings.

11:52.586 --> 11:53.879
Huh?

11:54.463 --> 11:56.632
I mean,

11:56.715 --> 11:59.802
I think you're very fortunate
to be able to openly express

12:00.428 --> 12:02.471
your love for something.

12:03.597 --> 12:04.640
You think so?

12:05.558 --> 12:07.893
I've never thought about that.

12:08.686 --> 12:10.062
Well,

12:10.146 --> 12:13.816
you and I come from different backgrounds.

12:15.067 --> 12:16.277
Backgrounds?

12:16.819 --> 12:17.820
Yeah.

12:19.363 --> 12:21.740
What I want to say
is that you're very lucky.

12:24.660 --> 12:26.829
All right, the ramyeon is ready.

12:27.413 --> 12:28.497
Let's eat.

12:28.581 --> 12:29.748
- Yeah.
- It's hot!

12:42.803 --> 12:44.138
Sakumoto?

12:44.221 --> 12:45.389
CHIEF MANAGER SAKUMOTO EIJI

12:45.473 --> 12:47.933
I work for a company called
Neo Meal Japan,

12:48.017 --> 12:51.270
and specialize in nutrition planning
and meal management for athletes.

12:56.275 --> 12:58.360
CONNECTING ATHLETES' MEALS
TO FUTURE PERFORMANCE

13:01.155 --> 13:03.699
NUTRIENTS MAKE UP THE BODY
STRENGTH COMES FROM DAILY MEALS

13:07.161 --> 13:12.458
SAKUMOTO EIJI

13:22.218 --> 13:23.260
The President's Award?

13:25.638 --> 13:26.805
That's right.

13:30.684 --> 13:32.937
She's on a roll.

13:35.064 --> 13:37.066
Hey, Rin. Have you seen this?

13:37.983 --> 13:39.151
What?

13:39.944 --> 13:43.447
As expected,
Amane won the President's Award.

13:44.031 --> 13:46.242
It's no surprise, I guess.

13:47.159 --> 13:48.661
There's an interview too.

13:48.744 --> 13:51.413
I don't know what my strength is but…

13:52.122 --> 13:55.000
I have never lost the urge
to create something,

13:55.084 --> 13:57.628
or forgotten the excitement.

13:57.711 --> 14:02.174
When I'm creating something,
I can't think about anything else.

14:02.258 --> 14:04.468
I don't even feel the need to eat…

14:04.552 --> 14:08.597
These are the kind of people
we call "creators," huh?

14:09.181 --> 14:11.600
I bet she's never run out of ideas
of what to make.

14:14.895 --> 14:19.400
If you had
an infinite amount of time and money,

14:19.483 --> 14:21.277
what would you like to create?

14:23.696 --> 14:24.822
Rin?

14:25.656 --> 14:26.824
Is something wrong?

14:28.033 --> 14:29.118
Huh?

14:30.494 --> 14:31.954
Um…

14:33.914 --> 14:34.874
Sorry…

14:36.625 --> 14:37.710
Rin?

14:47.511 --> 14:48.929
All right.

15:04.028 --> 15:05.362
I'm glad you got the day off today!

15:06.280 --> 15:07.865
Sorry for replying so late.

15:10.826 --> 15:13.329
Hey, everyone. Long time no see.

15:16.206 --> 15:18.167
- Man, that's brutal.
- Poor guy.

15:18.250 --> 15:20.628
He got an endorsement and he's a reserve?

15:24.131 --> 15:26.091
Hey, it's Taiga!

15:26.175 --> 15:28.928
- It's been so long!
- You never hang out with us!

15:29.011 --> 15:30.429
- Have a seat!
- Excuse me.

15:32.556 --> 15:35.392
- Oh right, you guys haven't seen him, huh?
- We haven't!

15:35.476 --> 15:37.353
- I have, here and there.
- What? Really?

15:37.436 --> 15:39.939
I went to ask because I didn't know.

15:40.564 --> 15:44.360
- But it had nothing to do with it!
- It didn't!

15:44.443 --> 15:46.695
- He just said that randomly.
- I know.

15:46.779 --> 15:49.073
They're different from back then,
aren't they?

15:49.156 --> 15:50.366
Yeah.

15:51.283 --> 15:54.161
When we were in college,

15:54.244 --> 15:56.288
we were all rivals.

15:56.372 --> 15:58.707
So we always felt tense around each other.

16:00.334 --> 16:03.963
Not just me, but probably all of them.

16:09.134 --> 16:12.137
Maybe I should have come here earlier.

16:14.306 --> 16:18.435
People aren't as involved
in your life, as much as you think.

16:18.978 --> 16:19.853
Yeah…

16:21.438 --> 16:23.607
And now was just the right timing,
I think.

16:24.900 --> 16:28.028
You look like you're doing
much better now compared to before.

16:29.822 --> 16:32.157
Isn't that because you found
something you want to do?

16:32.825 --> 16:34.284
Well…

16:35.703 --> 16:37.204
If that's the case,

16:38.330 --> 16:40.666
it wasn't my own doing.

16:42.084 --> 16:43.168
It was Rin.

16:43.919 --> 16:45.337
It's thanks to her.

16:46.880 --> 16:50.759
I was able to see things more positively
about myself.

16:53.220 --> 16:54.888
I see.

16:54.972 --> 16:56.765
Things are good with your girlfriend, huh?

16:59.476 --> 17:01.770
Not really, actually.

17:06.025 --> 17:07.860
What? You broke up?

17:10.070 --> 17:11.155
I'm not sure.

17:11.238 --> 17:13.407
I don't know, but…

17:14.783 --> 17:15.617
But?

17:17.327 --> 17:18.370
It's nothing.

17:50.611 --> 17:53.238
‪TANOMI

18:03.123 --> 18:04.458
So good!

18:05.292 --> 18:07.628
Your cooking is the best!

18:08.295 --> 18:09.671
It's so delicious!

18:15.594 --> 18:16.720
That's delicious.

18:18.931 --> 18:21.391
The flavors are incredible.

18:22.476 --> 18:24.144
Thank you.

18:24.228 --> 18:27.272
Why don't you deliver some to Rin
before you go to the party?

18:41.370 --> 18:42.913
JUN-HO

18:43.497 --> 18:46.250
I've been working hard
to become an animator.

18:46.333 --> 18:49.795
But you can't become one
just because you want to, right?

18:49.878 --> 18:51.088
I don't know.

18:51.171 --> 18:53.549
I want to believe in my talent
and challenge myself.

19:11.942 --> 19:13.235
Taiga…

19:34.631 --> 19:35.799
You're Rin's…

19:36.300 --> 19:38.677
- Long time no see--
- You guys broke up.

19:40.179 --> 19:41.513
What do you want?

19:45.976 --> 19:47.769
You didn't even bother contacting her.

19:48.687 --> 19:50.189
So what are you here for?

19:53.025 --> 19:54.443
Sorry…

19:56.278 --> 19:57.404
I just…

19:59.406 --> 20:00.908
wanted to see her.

20:02.910 --> 20:03.952
What?

20:06.955 --> 20:10.209
I came here today
without even thinking about…

20:12.669 --> 20:16.006
what to say if I actually saw Rin.

20:17.674 --> 20:18.967
To be honest,

20:19.760 --> 20:20.802
I still don't know.

20:24.681 --> 20:25.724
But…

20:26.725 --> 20:30.604
I thought that maybe
she would smile if she ate my cooking.

20:31.939 --> 20:33.565
That thought overpowered everything else.

20:39.112 --> 20:39.988
In the end…

20:42.407 --> 20:44.368
I didn't have the courage to see her.

20:46.620 --> 20:47.788
I'm pathetic.

20:54.336 --> 20:55.379
Rin is…

20:59.508 --> 21:01.009
a precious…

21:07.599 --> 21:08.934
little sister to me.

21:10.394 --> 21:14.648
So if you can't be responsible,
don't come near her ever again.

21:56.356 --> 21:57.858
Check the rest for me, okay?

21:57.941 --> 21:58.859
Yes.

21:58.942 --> 22:02.612
CLAYTON'S ANNIVERSARY PARTY

22:04.281 --> 22:05.115
Enjoy.

22:05.198 --> 22:06.241
Thank you.

22:06.825 --> 22:08.660
I'm cutting weight for my match right now,

22:08.744 --> 22:11.288
so it's really helpful
to know what's in the food.

22:11.371 --> 22:14.833
I can imagine.
Managing your diet must be hard.

22:14.916 --> 22:16.418
It really is.

22:16.501 --> 22:19.796
But this tastes good
and it's filling. I like it.

22:20.547 --> 22:22.424
Thank you. I'm glad.

22:22.507 --> 22:24.968
You're eating too much.
Leave some for everyone else.

22:25.052 --> 22:26.970
Jeez, let me eat.

22:27.054 --> 22:28.096
I'll come back.

22:32.184 --> 22:33.685
What do you want to try?

22:34.186 --> 22:35.604
I'm good.

22:35.687 --> 22:37.397
You're full already?

22:56.875 --> 22:58.752
Good to see you, Mr. Sakumoto.

22:59.294 --> 23:03.131
I'm Hase.
Ito introduced me to you a while ago.

23:03.215 --> 23:04.508
I remember.

23:05.634 --> 23:07.803
May I have some too?

23:08.595 --> 23:10.097
Yes, of course.

23:19.731 --> 23:20.690
Enjoy.

23:22.526 --> 23:23.693
Thank you.

23:39.084 --> 23:41.336
It has a very deep flavor.

23:43.421 --> 23:44.756
Thank you.

23:44.840 --> 23:46.341
I had heard

23:46.424 --> 23:49.636
that this dish was a hit last time,
so I was excited to try it.

23:50.262 --> 23:52.639
Yes, but…

23:53.181 --> 23:55.725
I changed it a bit from last time.

23:56.977 --> 23:58.186
The truth is,

23:58.895 --> 24:01.773
I used your website as a reference,

24:02.357 --> 24:07.112
and tried to make something that could
deliver both good flavor and nutrition.

24:07.863 --> 24:09.156
Really?

24:11.449 --> 24:14.578
But why did you choose a Korean dish?

24:15.245 --> 24:17.789
Do you have a connection with Korea?

24:19.708 --> 24:22.169
No, um…

24:24.087 --> 24:28.133
I guess you could say I was influenced
by someone important to me.

24:44.024 --> 24:45.233
Hello?

24:46.610 --> 24:48.236
You finally picked up.

24:49.487 --> 24:50.488
Sorry.

24:52.032 --> 24:53.533
Did you eat the food I left for you?

24:54.409 --> 24:55.327
Huh?

24:56.119 --> 24:57.621
It's hanging on your doorknob.

25:00.624 --> 25:01.833
Thank you.

25:03.543 --> 25:05.378
I'm sure that it will lift your spirits.

25:07.923 --> 25:09.049
Bye.

25:19.100 --> 25:22.354
IF YOU LIKE ME, EAT IT.

25:23.271 --> 25:28.610
To you
I hope I can be like the setting sun

25:29.611 --> 25:35.367
A fleeting, beautiful memory

25:36.034 --> 25:42.791
May our precious days of youth

25:42.874 --> 25:46.711
Remain in your heart
Like a gentle painting

25:46.795 --> 25:50.507
Filled with color

25:55.595 --> 26:01.893
And you, to me, a green, sorrowful melody

26:01.977 --> 26:08.441
That softly echoes in a corner of my heart

26:08.525 --> 26:14.823
I wish to be one of the stars

26:14.906 --> 26:21.371
That make your beautiful eyes
Shine eternally

26:21.454 --> 26:23.581
- Thank you for the food.
- May our

26:23.665 --> 26:28.378
Precious days of youth

26:28.461 --> 26:30.005
Remain in your heart

26:30.088 --> 26:32.132
- It's delicious.
- Like a gentle painting

26:32.215 --> 26:36.094
Filled with color
To you

26:36.177 --> 26:40.307
I hope I can be like the setting sun

26:41.224 --> 26:46.896
A fleeting, beautiful memory

26:47.480 --> 26:53.445
May our precious days of youth

26:54.404 --> 26:57.741
Remain in your heart
Like a gentle painting

26:57.824 --> 27:02.120
Filled with color

27:02.954 --> 27:04.372
Like a gentle painting

27:04.456 --> 27:11.129
Filled with color

27:22.807 --> 27:25.143
That was so moving!

27:25.226 --> 27:26.436
I didn't understand anything,

27:26.519 --> 27:28.104
but was that a love song?

27:29.022 --> 27:30.023
Yes.

27:31.149 --> 27:34.444
But for me,

27:35.528 --> 27:38.948
it's a farewell song, in a way.

27:40.825 --> 27:42.410
Thank you for the food.

27:49.376 --> 27:52.295
SLIDE TO ANSWER

27:53.838 --> 27:55.882
Yes? Hello?

27:57.759 --> 27:59.260
Yes, that's correct.

28:01.054 --> 28:01.888
What?

28:10.438 --> 28:11.731
Good work, Taiga.

28:11.815 --> 28:13.942
You too, Masumi.

28:14.025 --> 28:16.486
Want to get some drinks after this?

28:17.195 --> 28:18.905
No, I think I'll pass today.

28:18.988 --> 28:21.533
Okay. Maybe next time, then.

28:26.037 --> 28:27.330
Masumi.

28:30.625 --> 28:34.170
I really appreciate you
choosing me for this event.

28:35.755 --> 28:38.216
I was happy to be able
to engage with athletes

28:38.299 --> 28:40.260
in a different way than my college days.

28:41.553 --> 28:42.637
Yeah.

28:43.179 --> 28:47.058
I'm happy, too, to hear those words
coming from you.

28:47.892 --> 28:49.060
Thanks.

28:49.144 --> 28:50.103
Yeah.

28:56.526 --> 28:57.569
Hey…

28:58.486 --> 28:59.404
Huh?

28:59.988 --> 29:03.908
I'm sorry. I'm starting to like you again.

29:05.952 --> 29:07.036
What?

29:08.246 --> 29:10.749
I'm telling you,
because I don't want any more regrets.

29:11.833 --> 29:15.670
I do feel bad telling you this when things
aren't going well with your girlfriend.

29:18.965 --> 29:20.258
I feel like,

29:20.925 --> 29:23.261
this time,
we'll be able to support each other

29:23.344 --> 29:25.472
and make things work.

29:29.309 --> 29:30.518
Support?

29:31.478 --> 29:32.353
Yeah.

29:33.062 --> 29:34.439
Back then,

29:35.148 --> 29:37.901
I ignored your passion for track,

29:37.984 --> 29:39.861
and rushed you and hurt you.

29:42.113 --> 29:44.908
All I wanted was for you to say…

29:46.201 --> 29:49.120
I wish you would've accepted me,
even just for a second.

29:49.704 --> 29:50.914
Sorry.

29:52.457 --> 29:54.167
It's too difficult for me.

29:56.294 --> 29:58.087
I don't need an answer right away.

29:59.339 --> 30:00.340
Just think about it.

30:02.217 --> 30:03.426
Bye. Thanks for everything.

30:24.531 --> 30:27.992
RIN

32:34.619 --> 32:36.204
Taiga, I'm sorry.

32:40.500 --> 32:41.459
Rin!

32:50.802 --> 32:52.387
Finally, I found you!

32:52.470 --> 32:53.429
Thank goodness.

32:54.222 --> 32:55.264
Why?

32:56.849 --> 32:59.394
Rin? What's the matter?

33:11.739 --> 33:12.782
Are you okay?

33:25.920 --> 33:27.046
Taiga,

33:28.339 --> 33:30.550
why are you so nice?

33:32.051 --> 33:33.094
What?

33:34.929 --> 33:37.056
I said hurtful things to you.

33:38.558 --> 33:40.101
Well that's…

33:41.227 --> 33:43.312
because I made you say them, in a way.

33:46.357 --> 33:47.483
I…

33:48.234 --> 33:50.194
was too dependent on you.

33:50.945 --> 33:53.740
Thinking about my future
made me anxious and irritated,

33:54.532 --> 33:56.701
and I took all of it out on you.

33:59.787 --> 34:01.539
I'm really sorry.

34:08.212 --> 34:09.839
When I was in a rut,

34:10.798 --> 34:12.925
you never criticized me.

34:13.009 --> 34:16.471
You acknowledged my feelings
and encouraged me, remember?

34:18.681 --> 34:20.058
But when it was my turn,

34:21.684 --> 34:26.898
I pressured you and hurt you.

34:28.733 --> 34:29.859
I'm really sorry.

34:38.034 --> 34:39.869
Your words…

34:40.745 --> 34:41.996
Your smile…

34:43.706 --> 34:47.794
Everything about you gave me strength.

34:50.880 --> 34:52.548
So this time,

34:53.758 --> 34:56.886
I want to support you.

35:00.890 --> 35:02.016
I don't want…

35:05.019 --> 35:06.646
to let you go yet.

35:08.689 --> 35:09.690
That's…

35:12.235 --> 35:13.402
how I feel.

35:19.659 --> 35:20.827
Earlier,

35:22.954 --> 35:26.374
a person from an advertising agency who
praised my work at the cultural festival,

35:26.874 --> 35:28.209
called me.

35:29.460 --> 35:32.547
They asked if I wanted
to start working as an intern.

35:34.632 --> 35:36.217
That's great!

35:37.093 --> 35:38.678
Good for you!

35:42.140 --> 35:44.183
I wanted to tell you, Taiga.

35:46.060 --> 35:48.187
Whether I'm feeling sad,

35:49.063 --> 35:51.149
or feeling happy, or anything,

35:53.151 --> 35:55.653
the first person I think of is you.

35:56.737 --> 35:58.906
Everything brings me back to you.

36:03.744 --> 36:05.329
I like you, Taiga.

36:24.056 --> 36:25.224
Me too.

36:26.726 --> 36:28.644
I was thinking about you the whole time.

36:31.814 --> 36:35.359
I'm sorry for breaking up with you.

36:43.951 --> 36:44.952
Rin.

36:47.538 --> 36:52.251
Will you go out with me again?

36:56.547 --> 36:57.632
Yes.

37:10.561 --> 37:11.687
You're hungry?

37:13.314 --> 37:14.482
I'm hungry.

37:22.907 --> 37:24.158
Look, Rin!

37:26.285 --> 37:27.245
It stopped raining.

37:47.890 --> 37:49.767
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.024
It's good.

37:57.108 --> 37:59.235
We finally got to drink it.

37:59.318 --> 38:01.654
Taiga, thank you for the dak gomtang.

38:01.737 --> 38:03.239
It was really kkulmat!

38:05.116 --> 38:07.159
But did you know your Korean message said,

38:08.494 --> 38:11.122
"If you like me, eat it"

38:12.373 --> 38:13.249
in a commanding tone?

38:13.332 --> 38:14.625
What?

38:14.709 --> 38:15.710
It's okay

38:16.294 --> 38:19.130
if you want to act like a cocky guy
once in a while.

38:19.213 --> 38:20.047
Let's go.

38:21.924 --> 38:23.050
Where to?

38:23.134 --> 38:24.093
Home.

38:24.635 --> 38:25.761
What?

38:28.264 --> 38:29.890
Hey, wait!

38:32.935 --> 38:33.894
Are you making fun of me?

38:33.978 --> 38:34.812
It's a compliment.

38:34.895 --> 38:36.314
I like that about you.

38:36.397 --> 38:37.898
- Hey!
- Move.

38:37.982 --> 38:39.108
How stupid can you be?

38:39.191 --> 38:40.484
It's almost sad.

38:40.568 --> 38:41.402
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:41.485 --> 38:42.862
Thank you.

38:42.945 --> 38:43.821
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
